# Text files use LF line endings.
#
# `* text=auto` alone leaves normalization to a content heuristic, which can
# skip a file and turn a later edit into a whole-file line-ending diff. The
# explicit rules below pin the types this repository actually carries, so a
# blob's line endings do not depend on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`.
* text=auto

*.md text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Git hooks carry no extension, so `*.sh` misses them and `text=auto` would
# check them out CRLF on Windows, where the shebang then fails to resolve. A
# hook that cannot execute is a gate that does not gate.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
